<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="TAM 251" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2013" href="schedule/2013.xml">2013</calendarYear><term id="120138" href="schedule/2013/fall.xml">Fall 2013</term><subject id="TAM" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM.xml">Theoretical and Applied Mechanics</subject></parents><label>Introductory Solid Mechanics</label><description>Relationship between internal stresses and deformations produced by external forces acting on deformable bodies, and design principles based on mechanics of solids: normal stresses, shear stresses, and deformations produced by tensile, compressive, torsional, and bending loading of members; beam deflections; elastic energy and impact; multi-dimensional stress states; buckling of columns. Prerequisite: TAM 210 or TAM 211.</description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sections><section id="33294" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/33294.xml">ADA</section><section id="33381" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/33381.xml">ADB</section><section id="33482" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/33482.xml">ADC</section><section id="33532" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/33532.xml">ADD</section><section id="34913" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/34913.xml">ADE</section><section id="34924" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/34924.xml">ADF</section><section id="52451" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/52451.xml">ADG</section><section id="35217" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/35217.xml">AL1</section><section id="60900" href="schedule/2013/fall/TAM/251/60900.xml">AL3</section></sections></ns2:course>